  <main_text>
    <l n="1">rum[?] facta æstimare potest. Ut</l>
    <l n="2">pluris faciendum sit arbitrium</l>
    <l n="3">divinum, quam cujusdam ma-</l>
    <l n="4">le feriati judicium. Nam reve-</l>
    <l n="5">rentia quam Deo nostro &amp; ob-</l>
    <l n="6">sequium quod divinis præce-</l>
    <l n="7">ptis debemus, majus esse de-</l>
    <l n="8">bet, &amp; sanctius, quam ut cre-</l>
    <l n="9">aturæ morem gerere oporteat,</l>
    <l n="10">ad prava provocanti. Resp. 2.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Non amittit vel minimum ho-</l>
    <l n="12">noris gradum, qui temere, &amp;</l>
    <l n="13">contra omnia jura, divina at-</l>
    <l n="14">que humana, provocanti</l>
    <l n="15">non obtemperat. Neque in-</l>
    <l n="16">famis est, qui non sequitur in</l>
    <l n="17">certamen descendentem, quod</l>
    <l n="18">conscientiæ securitati ac tran-</l>
    <l n="19">quillitati velit consultum. Ut</l>
    <l n="20">adversæ parti merito dixerit:</l>
    <l n="21">Dæmonie perdat te robur tu-</l>
    <l n="22">um. Quinimo illi ipsi potius</l>
    <l n="23">famæ sunt prodigi, qui turpi-</l>
    <l n="24">ter adversus divina interdicta,</l>
    <l n="25">semetipsos ulciscuntur, &amp; de-</l>
    <l n="26">stinato consilio proximum læ-</l>
